      <h1>Introduction: Digital Controller Design</h1>
      <!--introduction-->
      <p>In this section, we will discuss converting continuous-time models into discrete-time (or difference equation) models. We
         will also introduce the z-transform and show how to use it to analyze and design controllers for discrete-time systems.
      </p>
      <p>Key MATLAB commands used in this tutorial are: <a href="http://www.mathworks.com/help/toolbox/control/ref/c2d.html"><tt>c2d</tt></a> , <a href="http://www.mathworks.com/help/toolbox/control/ref/pzmap.html"><tt>pzmap</tt></a> , <a href="http://www.mathworks.com/help/toolbox/control/ref/zgrid.html"><tt>zgrid</tt></a> , <a href="http://www.mathworks.com/help/toolbox/control/ref/step.html"><tt>step</tt></a> , <a href="http://www.mathworks.com/help/control/ref/rlocus.html"><tt>rlocus</tt></a></p>
      </div>
